      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HENLEY EXTREME (5) has raced herself into some good form, and steps up in class after a solid win by almost a length here 4 weeks ago over 1620m. She is ready to try a middle distance again, and an easy trial win since her last start will have her ready to run another big race. On top. NATIVE CLAN (3) whacked away for a fair fourth in a 5-horse field here 2 weeks ago over 2000m, after winning over this trip prior on this track. She will be looking for some early cover from a wide gate, but in another small field, she can bounce straight back into the top 3. REGAL HUNTER (4) won his last race over a middle distance 3 starts ago at Hobart, and has been in the money twice since then over 1600m. He is the likely pacemaker, and will again take plenty of catching. Stick with him. JOHNNIE PINCH (2) won't lack fitness, and with some cut in the ground, his winning chances will soar. Each way. RIPPINGTON (6) can make the most of an inside draw, and he will be trying this trip for the first time.",
